    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1813">

                <pb facs="1183" n="1067" xml:id="pg1067"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 823.00/181.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister McMillin to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Lima</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-05-27">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 27, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your telegram of May 26. I called upon Minister for Foreign Affairs to-day with
                    the Argentine and Brazilian Ministers and informed him the United States
                    recognizes the Government of Peru. Argentina and Brazil recognized at same time.
                    Joint action was appreciated. Chile has no representative here. News of proposed
                    recognition was telegraphed from Chile, appearing in this morning’s papers.
                    /</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">McMillin</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
